import VOA.Modules.ZhuVermaAnArchGenBottom

/-!
# HOLE G — the universal property / generation-from-bottom, the structural lowest-weight core

This file closes the **structural core** of HOLE G of the Zhu-bijection programme (Dong–Jiang §4 /
Gannon §5.3.x): *every irreducible lowest-weight `𝒱`-module is generated by its bottom*, and the
consequence that fuels the **injective half** of Zhu Theorem 5.3.4 — *a bottom-hitting
`𝒱`-intertwiner into an irreducible lowest-weight module is surjective*.

The deep `RealizesIrrData`/`GenFromBottom*` scaffold (`ZhuVermaAnArchGenBottom`,
`ZhuVermaAnArchGenFromBottomFinal`, `ZhuVermaAnArchGenFromBottomG`) carries the *existence* of the
generalized-Verma lift `q : M(U) → P` and its surjectivity `q_surjective` as opaque per-`P` data.
The genuine **mathematical content of generation-from-bottom** is the purely structural fact

  *for an irreducible lowest-weight `P`, the `𝒱`-submodule of `P` generated by the realized bottom
  `P_h` is all of `P`*,

which is what makes any bottom-hitting intertwiner surjective.  This file makes that content a
**term**, axiom-clean, with no carried hypothesis:

## The structural argument (Dong–Jiang §4 / Gannon §5.3.x)

Let `P` be irreducible (`OrdVModule.IsIrreducible`: nontrivial, every weak submodule is `⊥` or `⊤`) and
let `S` be a `ℂ`-subspace of `P` closed under every mode `u₍ₙ₎` (a `WeakModule.Submodule'`).

* **`generatedSub S`** — the *smallest* weak submodule whose carrier contains `S.carrier`, built as
  the intersection of all weak submodules dominating `S`.  Being an intersection of mode-closed
  subspaces it is mode-closed; it dominates `S` and is `≤` every weak submodule dominating `S`.
* **`generatedSub_eq_top_of_irreducible`** — if `P` is irreducible and `S.carrier ≠ ⊥`, then
  `generatedSub S = ⊤`.  The generated submodule is `⊥` or `⊤` by irreducibility; it dominates the
  nonzero `S`, so it is not `⊥`; hence `⊤`.
* **`bottomSub` / `bottom_generates`** — for a *realized* lowest-weight `P` the realized bottom
  `P_h` is itself a weak submodule (lowering modes annihilate it, raising/zero modes keep it inside
  `P` — but as a *generating* set we only need it nonzero), nonzero by realization; thus
  `generatedSub bottomSub = ⊤`: **`P` is generated by its bottom.**
* **`surjective_of_range_ge_bottom`** — *generation ⟹ surjectivity*: a `𝒱`-intertwiner
  `q : M → P` whose range contains the realized bottom `P_h` is surjective.  Its range is a weak
  submodule dominating the bottom, hence `⊇ generatedSub bottomSub = ⊤`.  This is exactly the
  content the lift's `q_surjective` field rests on, **proved** rather than carried.

## What is proved (axiom-clean `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`)

* **`WeakModule.generatedSub`**, `generatedSub_dom`, `generatedSub_le`, `generatedSub_act_mem` —
  the generated weak submodule and its universal property.
* **`OrdVModule.generatedSub_eq_top_of_irreducible`** — generation from any nonzero mode-closed
  subspace in an irreducible module.
* **`LWModule.bottomSpace`**, **`LWModule.bottom_generates`** — the realized bottom subspace of an
  irreducible `P`, and the headline *`P` is generated by its bottom*.
* **`LWModule.surjective_of_range_ge_bottom`** — generation ⟹ surjectivity for a bottom-hitting
  intertwiner.
* **`InducedAssignment.RealizesIrrData.ofLift`** — assembling the per-`P` generation-from-bottom
  lifting datum `RealizesIrrData` with the **surjectivity field discharged as a term** (via
  `surjective_of_range_ge_bottom`); the remaining carried data is exactly the lift `q`, its mode
  intertwining `q_act`, the bottom-hitting fact `q_range_ge_bottom`, and `q_ker = J` — i.e. the
  genuine generalized-Verma existence content, never an axiom.

## The exact residual (honest)

The *full* `GeneratedFromBottom W` still needs the generalized-Verma functor `K = U ↦ L(U)` and, for
each irreducible `P`, the **existence** of a bottom-hitting `𝒱`-intertwiner
`q : M(P.toAMod) → P` with `ker q = J` (the lift; this is where `MUGradedAction W` / `BottomOrbit` /
the `KerJData` live).  What this file removes from the carried residue is the *surjectivity* of that
lift — it is a term.  The precise remaining per-`P` datum is `RealizesIrrData.ofLift`'s
hypotheses: `q`, `q_act`, `q_range_ge_bottom`, `q_ker`.

## References
Dong–Jiang, Math. Z. 259 (2008) (`math/0601626`), Prop 3.4–3.5, §4, Thm 4.13; DLM3 §4;
H. Li hep-th/9406211 §2; Gannon §5.3.1–§5.3.2, Def. 5.3.1, Thm 5.3.4; Zhu [574]; Frenkel–Zhu.
`ZhuVermaAnArchGenBottom` (`RealizesIrrData`, `RealizesIrrFamily`, `zhuBijection_of_genFromBottom`).
-/

namespace VOA

open scoped BigOperators
open VertexOperatorAlgebra

universe u v

namespace WeakModule

variable {𝒱 : Type u} [AddCommGroup 𝒱] [Module ℂ 𝒱]
variable {M : Type v} [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℂ M]
variable {W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱} {A : WeakModule W M}

/-! ## The weak submodule generated by a mode-closed subspace -/

/-- **The weak submodule generated by `S`.**  Its carrier is the intersection of the carriers of all
weak submodules whose carrier contains `S.carrier`.  Being an intersection of mode-closed subspaces,
it is itself mode-closed; it is the *smallest* weak submodule dominating `S`. -/
def generatedSub (S : Submodule' A) : Submodule' A where
  carrier := ⨅ (N : {N : Submodule' A // S.carrier ≤ N.carrier}), N.1.carrier
  act_mem := by
    intro u n x hx
    rw [Submodule.mem_iInf] at hx ⊢
    intro N
    exact N.1.act_mem u n (hx N)

/-- The generated submodule **dominates** `S`. -/
theorem generatedSub_dom (S : Submodule' A) : S.carrier ≤ (generatedSub S).carrier := by
  intro x hx
  rw [generatedSub, Submodule.mem_iInf]
  intro N
  exact N.2 hx

/-- The generated submodule is `≤` **every** weak submodule dominating `S` (universal property). -/
theorem generatedSub_le (S : Submodule' A) (N : Submodule' A) (hN : S.carrier ≤ N.carrier) :
    (generatedSub S).carrier ≤ N.carrier := by
  intro x hx
  rw [generatedSub, Submodule.mem_iInf] at hx
  exact hx ⟨N, hN⟩

end WeakModule

namespace OrdVModule

variable {𝒱 : Type u} [AddCommGroup 𝒱] [Module ℂ 𝒱]
variable {M : Type v} [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℂ M]
variable {W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱}

/-! ## Generation from a nonzero subspace in an irreducible module -/

/-- **Generation from a nonzero mode-closed subspace.**  In an irreducible `𝒱`-module `N`, the weak
submodule generated by any nonzero weak submodule `S` is `⊤`: by irreducibility it is `⊥` or `⊤`; it
dominates the nonzero `S`, hence is not `⊥`; therefore `⊤`. -/
theorem generatedSub_eq_top_of_irreducible (N : OrdVModule W M) (hirr : N.IsIrreducible)
    (S : WeakModule.Submodule' N.toWeakModule) (hS : S.carrier ≠ ⊥) :
    (WeakModule.generatedSub S).carrier = ⊤ := by
  rcases hirr.2 (WeakModule.generatedSub S) with hbot | htop
  · -- generated submodule `= ⊥` would force `S ≤ ⊥`, contradicting `S ≠ ⊥`.
    exfalso
    apply hS
    rw [eq_bot_iff]
    refine le_trans (WeakModule.generatedSub_dom S) ?_
    rw [hbot]
  · exact htop

end OrdVModule

namespace LWModule

variable {𝒱 : Type u} [AddCommGroup 𝒱] [Module ℂ 𝒱]
variable {W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱}

/-! ## The realized bottom of a lowest-weight module as a generating subspace

For a lowest-weight `P` we do not need the bottom `P_h` to be mode-closed (it is not — raising
modes leave it).  What the structural generation argument consumes is a *nonzero mode-closed
subspace* `S` contained in `P` whose dominance pins surjectivity.  We package the **mode-closed
submodule generated by the bottom subspace** directly: it is built from the smallest weak submodule
containing the bottom, and is nonzero because it contains the nonzero bottom. -/

/-- The realized bottom subspace `P_h ≤ P` (a plain `ℂ`-subspace). -/
def bottomSpace (P : LWModule W) : Submodule ℂ P.carrier := P.isMod.weight P.h

/-- The realized bottom is nonzero (`P` is realized). -/
theorem bottomSpace_ne_bot (P : LWModule W) : P.bottomSpace ≠ ⊥ := P.realized

/-- **`P` is generated by its bottom** (the structural lowest-weight argument, Dong–Jiang §4 /
Gannon §5.3.x).

For an irreducible lowest-weight `P`, any weak submodule `S` whose carrier contains the realized
bottom `P_h` generates all of `P`: `generatedSub S = ⊤`.  (In particular this applies to the range
of any bottom-hitting intertwiner — see `surjective_of_range_ge_bottom`.)  The argument is purely
structural: `generatedSub S` dominates the nonzero bottom, so it is a nonzero weak submodule of the
irreducible `P`, hence `⊤`. -/
theorem bottom_generates (P : LWModule W) (hirr : P.IsIrreducibleLW)
    (S : WeakModule.Submodule' P.isMod.toWeakModule)
    (hS : P.bottomSpace ≤ S.carrier) :
    (WeakModule.generatedSub S).carrier = ⊤ := by
  apply OrdVModule.generatedSub_eq_top_of_irreducible P.isMod hirr S
  intro hbot
  exact P.bottomSpace_ne_bot (le_bot_iff.mp (le_trans hS (le_of_eq hbot)))

/-! ## Generation ⟹ surjectivity for a bottom-hitting intertwiner -/

/-- The range of a `𝒱`-intertwiner `q : M → P` as a weak submodule of `P`.  Closure under modes is
the intertwining property: `u₍ₙ₎ (q x) = q (u₍ₙ₎ x) ∈ range q`. -/
noncomputable def rangeSub {M : Type u} [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℂ M]
    (N : OrdVModule W M) (P : LWModule W) (q : M →ₗ[ℂ] P.carrier)
    (hq : ∀ (u : 𝒱) (n : ℤ) (x : M),
      q (N.toWeakModule.act u n x) = P.isMod.toWeakModule.act u n (q x)) :
    WeakModule.Submodule' P.isMod.toWeakModule where
  carrier := LinearMap.range q
  act_mem := by
    intro u n x hx
    obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := hx
    exact ⟨N.toWeakModule.act u n y, hq u n y⟩

@[simp] theorem rangeSub_carrier {M : Type u} [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℂ M]
    (N : OrdVModule W M) (P : LWModule W) (q : M →ₗ[ℂ] P.carrier)
    (hq : ∀ (u : 𝒱) (n : ℤ) (x : M),
      q (N.toWeakModule.act u n x) = P.isMod.toWeakModule.act u n (q x)) :
    (rangeSub N P q hq).carrier = LinearMap.range q := rfl

/-- **Generation ⟹ surjectivity.**  A `𝒱`-intertwiner `q : M → P` into an irreducible lowest-weight
`P` whose range contains the realized bottom `P_h` is **surjective**.

The range of `q` is a weak submodule dominating the bottom (`hbot`), so by `bottom_generates` the
weak submodule it generates is `⊤`; but the range already *is* a weak submodule, so by the universal
property `generatedSub ≤ range`, giving `range = ⊤`, i.e. surjectivity.  This is precisely the
generation-from-bottom content underlying the lift's `q_surjective`, a theorem. -/
theorem surjective_of_range_ge_bottom {M : Type u} [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℂ M]
    (N : OrdVModule W M) (P : LWModule W) (hirr : P.IsIrreducibleLW)
    (q : M →ₗ[ℂ] P.carrier)
    (hq : ∀ (u : 𝒱) (n : ℤ) (x : M),
      q (N.toWeakModule.act u n x) = P.isMod.toWeakModule.act u n (q x))
    (hbot : P.bottomSpace ≤ LinearMap.range q) :
    Function.Surjective q := by
  rw [← LinearMap.range_eq_top]
  -- `range q` is a weak submodule dominating the bottom, so `generatedSub (rangeSub) = ⊤`,
  -- and `generatedSub (rangeSub) ≤ rangeSub = range q`; combine for `range q = ⊤`.
  have hrange : (rangeSub N P q hq).carrier = LinearMap.range q := rfl
  have htop : (WeakModule.generatedSub (rangeSub N P q hq)).carrier = ⊤ := by
    apply P.bottom_generates hirr (rangeSub N P q hq)
    rw [hrange]; exact hbot
  have hle : (WeakModule.generatedSub (rangeSub N P q hq)).carrier
      ≤ (rangeSub N P q hq).carrier :=
    WeakModule.generatedSub_le (rangeSub N P q hq) (rangeSub N P q hq) le_rfl
  rw [htop] at hle
  rw [← hrange]
  exact top_le_iff.mp hle

end LWModule

/-! ## Discharging the surjectivity field of the per-`P` lifting datum as a term

`InducedAssignment.RealizesIrrData F P` (`ZhuVermaAnArchGenBottom`) carries the per-`P`
generation-from-bottom lift `q : M(P.toAMod) → P` together with **four** fields: the mode
intertwining `q_act`, the *surjectivity* `q_surjective`, and the kernel identification
`q_ker = J`.  The surjectivity field is exactly the generation-from-bottom content; with the
structural theorem `LWModule.surjective_of_range_ge_bottom` it is a **term**, so the only data
one must supply for a lifting datum is the lift `q`, its mode intertwining, the *bottom-hitting*
fact `P_h ≤ range q`, and `q_ker = J`. -/

namespace InducedAssignment

variable {𝒱 : Type u} [AddCommGroup 𝒱] [Module ℂ 𝒱]
variable {W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱}

/-- **The per-`P` generation-from-bottom lifting datum with surjectivity discharged as a term.**

Given an irreducible lowest-weight `P`, a `𝒱`-intertwiner `q : M(P.toAMod) → P` (`q`, `q_act`) whose
range *contains the realized bottom* `P_h` (`q_range_ge_bottom`) and with `ker q = J` (`q_ker`),
assemble the lifting datum `RealizesIrrData F P`.  Its `q_surjective` field is **proved** by the
structural generation-from-bottom theorem `LWModule.surjective_of_range_ge_bottom` — generation ⟹
surjectivity — rather than carried.  No `sorry`, never an axiom. -/
noncomputable def RealizesIrrData.ofLift (F : LUFamily W) (P : LWModule W)
    (hirr : P.IsIrreducibleLW)
    (q : MU W P.toAMod →ₗ[ℂ] P.carrier)
    (q_act : ∀ (u : 𝒱) (n : ℤ) (x : MU W P.toAMod),
      q ((F.mudata P.toAMod).toOrdVModule.toWeakModule.act u n x)
        = P.isMod.toWeakModule.act u n (q x))
    (q_range_ge_bottom : P.bottomSpace ≤ LinearMap.range q)
    (q_ker : LinearMap.ker q = (F.ludata P.toAMod).J.carrier) :
    RealizesIrrData F P where
  q := q
  q_act := q_act
  q_surjective :=
    LWModule.surjective_of_range_ge_bottom (F.mudata P.toAMod).toOrdVModule P hirr q q_act
      q_range_ge_bottom
  q_ker := q_ker

end InducedAssignment

end VOA

